//Description:
//The purpose of the Loader Check Zone (LCZ) is to correct faulty loaded carriers.
//This is important in order to prevent damage to baggage and equipment.
//The LCZ consists of a transport sections (TRS) a transfer (TTS/TSS) and a
//operator object (OPO).
//The OPO itself is not part of this block, but has an interface to this block.
//If the envelope is not OK, it will be mark with a contour fault by the upstream CHO
//and the carrier needs to be sorted, stopped and corrected. If needed the operator can
//request an empty carrier for the LCZ.
//The LCZ will send the LNK of a arriving carrier to the OPO to let the OPO determine
//if the carrier has to be sorted and stopped. The LCZ will sort and stop carriers which
//have an arrived location which matches the local destination of the LCZ on the OPO position.
//For these carriers the LCZ will send the LNK again to the OPO. The OPO will take care of
//updating the carrier information on dispatch and send a dispatch request to the LCZ.
//After dispatch the carrier will be merged into to main stream.
//In case of an OPO error the OPO will request the LCZ to halt.
   VAR_INPUT 
      i_ID : DWord;   // ID Record HEX AAAAZZSS/OO
      i_CMD_Enable : Bool;   // CMD: Enable command
      i_CMD_Start : Bool;   // CMD: Start command
      i_CMD_Reset : Bool;   // CMD: Reset command
      i_CMD_Controlled_Stop : Bool;   // CMD: Controlled stop command
      i_IO_Available : Bool;   // IO is OK signal (no fieldbus or IO error)
      i_Safety_OK : Bool;   // Safety is OK signal
